{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790572287,"nonce":"Zl1u6YH/yYVYzHnmdMUYz1RahIM=","title":"Task: a fresh clone can pull; a not-yet-merged identity doesn't abort the merge","message":"A fresh clone could never pull: every `git work pull` printed\n`merge error: identity doesn't exist` five times and merged nothing,\nleaving `refs/work-users`, `refs/work-issues` and `refs/work-schema` empty\nwhile the remote-tracking copies sat fetched and ready.\n\nThe pull deadlocked against itself. `SubCache.MergeAll` resolves the merge\nauthor up front and tolerated only `identity.ErrNoIdentitySet`. A clone whose\n`git-bug.identity` is set but whose `refs/work-users/\u003cid\u003e` has not been merged\nyet gets `entity.ErrNotFound` instead, so the guard emitted a merge error and\nreturned before merging anything. That guard runs in all five subcaches, so the\nidentity tier — which exists precisely to copy that ref out of\n`refs/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/work-users` — aborted along with the rest, and the state\ncould never repair itself.\n\nThe comment above the guard already said the author is only needed for merge\ncommits and so is optional; the check was just too narrow. Tolerate\n`entity.ErrNotFound` as well, via `entity.IsErrNotFound` — `ErrNotFound` is a\npointer type with no `Is` method, so `errors.Is` would never match it.\n\nVerified on a clone stuck in exactly that state, with the stale config left in\nplace: the pull merged 2 identities, 98 issues and 82 schema entities, and\n`git work user me` and `git work issue` work afterwards.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["core"],"parent":"bc14d4d88d377f01d8cdafffc35fa0ee11b5b4795ec8034742de3e1cc15858ac","priority":"high","status":"done","type":"task"}}]}